76c89f50-bff2-4715-8ca6-8c4bfc88c591	36f398d4-d44f-4447-a691-6e47f4b457b9	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	2	):\nWell maintained but seasonal challenges: winter closures, ferry requirements, and strict axle weight enforcement.\n\n\n3. Routing Tools and Software\n3.1 Professional Routing Software (Truck-Specific)\nStandard navigation applications such as Google Maps or Waze are not appropriate for commercial truck routing in Europe. They do not account for vehicle-specific restrictions. Dispatchers must use professional tools:\n\nSoftware\nBest Used For\nKey Features\nPTV Navigator / PTV Map&Guide\nPan-European routing\nWeight, height, ADR restrictions; toll calculation; driving bans\nHERE WeGo Truck\nReal-time navigation\nLive traffic, hazmat routes, bridge limits\nSygic Truck GPS\nDriver navigation\nOffline maps, trailer profiles, parking spots\nTomTom Telematics\nFleet tracking + routing\nLive ETA updates, geofencing, fuel analytics\nTransporeon / FourKites\nLoad visibility & tendering\nReal-time shipment tracking, ETA prediction\n\n3.2 How to Build a Route in PTV Map&Guide\nStep-by-Step Route Creation\nWhen planning a route using PTV Map&Guide or a similar platform, follow this sequence consistently:\n Enter vehicle profile: Gross vehicle weight (GVW), axle count, height, width, length, and cargo type (standard, ADR, temperature-controlled).\n Set departure date and time: The system will calculate driving bans and suggest the optimal start window.\n Enter waypoints in order: Origin ? intermediate stops (if any) ? destination. Use postal codes for accuracy.\n Review toll costs: Check country-by-country toll breakdown and compare against rate to ensure profitability.\n Check for restrictions: Review any height, weight, or hazmat restrictions flagged on the route before sending to driver.\n Export or share: Share route via TMS, email, or directly to driver's navigation device.\n\n? Note: Never send a driver a route without first verifying the vehicle profile is correctly set. A wrong vehicle height or weight entry can route a truck under a low bridge or onto a road with prohibited axle loads.\n\n3.3 Digital Load Boards in Europe\nLoad boards are online marketplaces where brokers and shippers post available freight. The main platforms active in the European market are:\n TimoCom (TC Truck & Cargo):\nThe largest European load board with over 750,000 transport offers daily. Available in 44 countries.\n Transopedia:\nStrong presence in	500	[-0.032165527,-0.023391724,-0.018630981,0.0046577454,-0.015113831,0.0087890625,0.01411438,0.02218628,-0.05923462,0.021469116,0.0635376,0.0054092407,-0.031433105,0.015167236,-0.027954102,0.016647339,0.008712769,-0.03314209,0.023345947,-0.03491211,0.029586792,0.042114258,-0.016784668,-0.007007599,0.0007863045,-0.02154541,0.04522705,-0.012580872,-0.01763916,0.0335083,0.020553589,0.043823242,-0.010421753,-0.0067977905,0.027267456,-0.043182373,0.017562866,0.0029067993,-0.0018014908,0.037231445,0.03363037,0.002691269,0.018249512,0.040252686,-0.016921997,-0.0104522705,-0.031097412,0.013519287,0.021072388,-0.0095825195,-0.042236328,-0.056030273,-0.011390686,0.01991272,0.022903442,0.028320312,0.014312744,0.117492676,-0.003921509,0.00724411,0.00111866,-0.029174805,-0.0048065186,-0.028198242,-0.04421997,0.043640137,-0.017990112,0.02456665,-0.05960083,-0.018051147,-0.0625,0.021316528,-0.018661499,0.033996582,-0.01260376,-0.021331787,-0.006011963,0.019546509,0.034423828,0.041503906,0.04232788,0.033355713,-0.019104004,-0.04550171,0.0062828064,-0.014266968,-0.051971436,-0.10852051,0.033081055,0.0046310425,0.018707275,-0.0004310608,-0.03161621,-0.011383057,0.030914307,0.0046920776,-0.0093688965,0.005329132,0.030258179,0.007434845,-0.0021018982,-0.043914795,0.011131287,-0.019256592,0.023330688,-0.045196533,0.029510498,0.024398804,-0.0054016113,0.041778564,0.051971436,0.009674072,0.028137207,0.0309906,-0.03778076,-0.040222168,-0.028396606,-0.078552246,0.05026245,0.009849548,-0.034698486,0.0034542084,0