7141f81f-30fa-4a1c-bf47-8ea3ac0cda5c	36f398d4-d44f-4447-a691-6e47f4b457b9	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	6	SS Toll System)\nGermany operates one of Europe's most advanced truck toll systems. As of December 2023, it expanded to all federal roads (Bundesstraßen), not just motorways. Key points for dispatchers:\n Applies to all trucks over 3.5 tonnes GVW on German motorways and federal roads.\n Rate is calculated per km, based on EURO emission class, number of axles, and distance.\n A certified on-board unit (OBU) must be installed in the truck. Tolling device providers include: DKV, Toll Collect, and UTA.\n EURO 6 trucks receive the lowest toll rates; EURO 5 and below pay progressively higher rates.\n CO2 emission surcharge introduced in 2024  an additional charge per tonne of CO2 emitted.\n\n?  For a Germany transit trip (e.g., Rotterdam ? Warsaw via A2), toll costs for a Euro 6 truck typically range between 180280 depending on routing. Always check current rates at toll-collect.de.\n\n5.3 France  Autoroutes (Toll Booths)\nFrance has the most extensive toll motorway network in Europe, covering over 9,000 km. Dispatchers should know:\n Heavy trucks (over 3.5t) pay higher rates than passenger vehicles  typically 24x the car rate.\n The Liber-t / Télépéage transponder system (compatible with most major European transponder providers) allows barrier-free payment.\n Major providers of compatible transponders: Axxes, DKV, UTA, Eurotoll.\n High-frequency routes such as ParisLyon, LyonMarseille, and ParisLille are heavily tolled.\n Summer surcharges ('Peak hour rates') apply on select routes in July and August.\n\n5.4 Switzerland  Special Case\nSwitzerland is not an EU member but is a critical transit country between Northern and Southern Europe. The Swiss Heavy Vehicle Fee (LSVA / PSVA) is unique:\n Applied to all trucks over 3.5t using Swiss roads, regardless of nationality.\n Calculated based on: total distance driven in Switzerland × GVW × em