6ea423c9-49f7-4732-89b9-6126ab28654b	5095ed8e-5ad2-411f-8ebd-3df935ca98fa	1657d178-a9b9-4181-b98d-db2709ce44a6	0	\nDISPATCHER TRAINING PROGRAM\nLoad Planning & Routing\nEuropean Market Edition\n\n\nConfidential  Internal Training Document\nVersion 1.0 | 2024\n\n\n1. Introduction to Load Planning in Europe\nLoad planning and routing in the European market requires a thorough understanding of a complex, multi-country logistics environment. Unlike domestic trucking, European dispatchers must navigate diverse regulatory frameworks, multiple languages, border crossing procedures, and a dense network of roads spanning over 40 countries. This module equips new dispatchers with the foundational knowledge and practical skills needed to plan loads and routes efficiently, legally, and profitably across Europe.\n\n1.1 Why European Load Planning Is Unique\nThe European freight market operates within a patchwork of national regulations, tolling systems, and infrastructure standards. A dispatcher working European lanes must simultaneously consider:\n Cabotage restrictions limiting how many loads a foreign carrier can perform within a single country\n Country-specific driving bans on weekends, public holidays, and during peak traffic periods\n Multiple currency and toll systems (Euros, Swiss Francs, UK Pounds, Scandinavian currencies)\n Varying axle load and dimension limits across member states\n Language barriers in communication with drivers, shippers, and receivers\n Different legal systems for contract enforcement and liability\n\n?  The European road freight market moves approximately 1.8 billion tonnes of goods per year. Germany, France, Poland, Spain, and the Netherlands are the five largest freight markets by volume.\n\n2. The European Road Network\n2.1 Key Corridors and Motorway Networks\nEurope is served by a series of major international road corridors that form the backbone of cross-border trucking. Understanding these corridors enables dispatchers to select optimal routes quickly.\n\nE-Road / Motorway\nKey Countries Covered\nStrategic Importance\nE40 (A4/E40)\nBelgium ? Germany ? Poland ? Ukraine\nMain east-west backbone\nE35 (A1/A5)\nNetherlands ? Germany ? Switzerland ? Italy\nNorth-south spine\nE17 (A14/A7)\nUK Channel ports ? Belgium ? France\nUK/Ireland freight gateway\nE55\nGermany ? Czechia ? Austria ? Greece\nBalkan corridor\nE75\nFinland ? Hungary ? Greece\nNordic-Mediterranean link\nE80 (A10/AP7)\nPortugal ? Spain ? France ? Turkey\nIberian & southern corridor	500	[-0.017059326,-0.01802063,-0.020889282,0.029510498,-0.0647583,-0.018005371,0.014030457,0.038635254,-0.070373535,0.013618469,0.028503418,-0.0073394775,-0.0014019012,-0.022994995,-0.042053223,0.016036987,-0.021713257,-0.03842163,0.0070533752,-0.028869629,0.041290283,0.055145264,-0.037384033,0.011123657,-0.024230957,-0.005458832,0.015213013,-0.0015974045,-0.006500244,0.011802673,0.013671875,0.05722046,0.0012273788,-0.029037476,0.03326416,-0.030685425,-0.006629944,0.014694214,-0.017318726,0.03189087,0.019515991,0.009750366,0.0022010803,0.06970215,0.013259888,-0.02696228,-0.032226562,0.031463623,-0.011161804,-0.012779236,-0.022232056,-0.08526611,-0.026473999,-0.00182724,-0.0035266876,-0.00497818,-0.005176544,0.06304932,0.004589081,0.019760132,-0.022476196,-0.03567505,0.0059814453,-0.036346436,-0.061187744,0.050811768,-0.001821518,0.046325684,-0.032104492,-0.01763916,-0.04473877,0.024780273,-0.01878357,0.046173096,-0.0029907227,-0.02986145,0.00032138824,0.022033691,0.043060303,0.0234375,0.02671814,0.02444458,-0.019119263,-0.016418457,0.048736572,-0.004875183,-0.035858154,-0.11212158,0.04296875,0.012237549,-0.002231598,-0.016296387,-0.046539307,-0.022079468,-0.0029468536,0.028274536,0.01687622,-0.021240234,0.027038574,0.016799927,0.017044067,0.008987427,0.0005235672,0.022598267,0.056365967,-0.019851685,0.015853882,0.009605408,0.00062942505,0.05493164,0.06896973,-0.014755249,0.0070114136,0.059936523,-0.033294678,-0.05166626,-0.029541016,-0.09069824,0.07354736,