27153d2d-804a-485e-9532-154c641483f2	5095ed8e-5ad2-411f-8ebd-3df935ca98fa	1657d178-a9b9-4181-b98d-db2709ce44a6	2	):\nWell maintained but seasonal challenges: winter closures, ferry requirements, and strict axle weight enforcement.\n\n\n3. Routing Tools and Software\n3.1 Professional Routing Software (Truck-Specific)\nStandard navigation applications such as Google Maps or Waze are not appropriate for commercial truck routing in Europe. They do not account for vehicle-specific restrictions. Dispatchers must use professional tools:\n\nSoftware\nBest Used For\nKey Features\nPTV Navigator / PTV Map&Guide\nPan-European routing\nWeight, height, ADR restrictions; toll calculation; driving bans\nHERE WeGo Truck\nReal-time navigation\nLive traffic, hazmat routes, bridge limits\nSygic Truck GPS\nDriver navigation\nOffline maps, trailer profiles, parking spots\nTomTom Telematics\nFleet tracking + routing\nLive ETA updates, geofencing, fuel analytics\nTransporeon / FourKites\nLoad visibility & tendering\nReal-time shipment tracking, ETA prediction\n\n3.2 How to Build a Route in PTV Map&Guide\nStep-by-Step Route Creation\nWhen planning a route using PTV Map&Guide or a similar platform, follow this sequence consistently:\n Enter vehicle profile: Gross vehicle weight (GVW), axle count, height, width, length, and cargo type (standard, ADR, temperature-controlled).\n Set departure date and time: The system will calculate driving bans and suggest the optimal start window.\n Enter waypoints in order: Origin ? intermediate stops (if any) ? destination. Use postal codes for accuracy.\n Review toll costs: Check country-by-country toll breakdown and compare against rate to ensure profitability.\n Check for restrictions: Review any height, weight, or hazmat restrictions flagged on the route before sending to driver.\n Export or share: Share route via TMS, email, or directly to driver's navigation device.\n\n? Note: Never send a driver a route without first verifying the vehicle profi