9470b2a2-9500-40b3-aa0c-3b44c582ac26	5095ed8e-5ad2-411f-8ebd-3df935ca98fa	1657d178-a9b9-4181-b98d-db2709ce44a6	9	.\nBox / Closed Van\nHigh-value goods, electronics, clothing, pharma\nSide doors only. Better security and weather protection.\nReefer (Refrigerated)\nFood, pharmaceuticals, flowers, temperature-sensitive cargo\nATP cert required. Fuel for refrigeration unit adds to costs.\nFlatbed / Lowloader\nMachinery, steel, oversized industrial equipment\nMay require escort, special permit, and route survey.\nTanker (Liquid)\nChemicals, food liquids, fuel, powders\nADR certification often required. Product contamination rules apply.\nMega Trailer (Jumbo)\nHigh-volume, low-weight cargo (textiles, packaging)\nInternal height up to 3m. Only allowed in select countries (NL, BE, DE, PL).\nDouble-deck\nAutomotive parts, light packaged goods\nHeight limit applies. Loading is complex  allow extra time.\n\n\n\n7. Border Crossings and Documentation\n7.1 Intra-EU Border Crossings\nTravel between Schengen Area member states generally requires no customs stops  trucks pass freely. However, dispatchers must still be aware of:\n Random police controls can occur at any border  ensure all documentation is always complete and accessible.\n Some non-Schengen EU countries (Romania, Bulgaria, Croatia, Ireland) have border controls  plan for delays especially when these countries finalise Schengen accession.\n Local road authorities may operate weigh stations at border regions  ensure load compliance is verified before departure.\n\n7.2 Non-EU Border Crossings\nCrossings into or out of non-EU countries (Switzerland, UK, Norway, Turkey, Ukraine, Western Balkans) require full customs documentation and often have significant wait times. Plan extra time into any schedule involving these borders.\n\nRequired Documents for International Loads\nDocument\nPurpose & Notes\nCMR Waybill\nInternational consignment note under the CMR Convention. Required for all international road freight. 4 copies minimum (driver, carrier, sender, receiver).\nCommercial Invoice\nStates the value, origin, and description of goods. Required for customs in non-EU/non-Schengen crossings.\nPacking List\nDetails number of packages, dimensions, and weights. Accompanies the commercial invoice.\nEUR.1 / T1 / T2 Movement Certificate\nCustoms status document for EU origin goods. Required for Switzerland, Norway, and non-EU countries.\nADR Documentation\nFor hazardous goods: safety	500	[-0.020080566,-0.0061798096,-0.005378723,0.019470215,-0.035369873,-0.023895264,0.015029907,0.021209717,-0.053009033,-0.0082092285,0.042266846,-0.031829834,-0.025024414,-0.038879395,-0.02760315,-0.0003142357,0.01689148,-0.017684937,0.031402588,-0.04006958,0.015609741,0.07171631,-0.0046539307,-0.022399902,0.012763977,-0.0099487305,0.043151855,-0.015327454,-0.01171875,0.007850647,-0.008644104,0.027450562,-0.015914917,0.00091695786,0.055236816,-0.008255005,0.03555298,0.03363037,-0.003063202,-0.0027542114,0.049560547,0.014511108,-0.011627197,0.06536865,-0.029647827,0.0014753342,-0.038726807,0.01701355,-0.017654419,-0.004005432,-0.034606934,-0.061523438,-0.013969421,-0.030578613,0.011100769,0.035614014,-0.013015747,0.10040283,-0.010559082,-0.0056762695,-0.024520874,-0.021896362,-0.011795044,-0.014099121,-0.045928955,0.03717041,-0.0017824173,0.012207031,-0.069885254,-0.021652222,-0.087646484,0.041046143,-0.024276733,0.037261963,-0.014526367,0.004463196,0.04788208,0.033996582,0.047546387,0.035186768,0.035064697,0.045074463,0.05609131,0.0045318604,-0.01651001,-0.008125305,-0.058776855,-0.10070801,0.03591919,-0.012336731,0.00043559074,-0.0184021,-0.017532349,0.0013036728,0.015991211,0.0042304993,-0.012565613,0.008201599,0.016021729,-0.0107421875,0.0061912537,-0.020629883,0.01133728,-0.021118164,0.03866577,-0.044403076,0.06097412,0.0020103455,-0.03768921,0.039611816,0.04336548,0.006969452,0.013885498,0.047454834,7.724762e-05,-0.036712646,-0.02947998,-0.055023193,0.029434204,0.039367676,-0.028289795,-0.006732940