d3590fc7-3a68-4f85-b9df-c2f1aeea1a46	59050f63-61ce-4125-9dc1-8c1b20f09f54	7ba430b5-849e-48e7-aba9-902af6db4577	1	 ? Greece\nBalkan corridor\nE75\nFinland ? Hungary ? Greece\nNordic-Mediterranean link\nE80 (A10/AP7)\nPortugal ? Spain ? France ? Turkey\nIberian & southern corridor\n\n2.2 Major Freight Hubs and Logistics Parks\nPlanning routes efficiently requires knowledge of where drivers can load, unload, swap trailers, and rest. The following hubs are critical reference points:\n\n Port of Rotterdam: Rotterdam (Netherlands)\nEurope's largest port. Gateway for deep-sea imports/exports. Critical for intermodal connections.\n Hamburg (Germany):\nSecond largest European port. Major hub for Nordic and Eastern European distribution.\n Duisburg (Germany):\nLargest inland port in the world. The terminus of the China-Europe rail corridor.\n Lyon (France):\nCentral logistics hub connecting Iberia to Northern and Eastern Europe.\n Verona / Bologna (Italy):\nKey gateways for Italian industrial goods moving north.\n Warsaw / ?ód? (Poland):\nFastest growing logistics region in Europe, serving Eastern EU markets.\n\n? Note: Always check if your shipper or receiver is located in or near a Logistics Park (e.g. GLP, Prologis, MLP). These parks may have specific entry procedures, appointment systems, and restricted hours.\n\n2.3 Road Quality and Infrastructure Awareness\nRoad infrastructure quality varies considerably across Europe. Dispatchers must account for:\n Western Europe (DE, NL, BE, AT, FR):\nGenerally excellent motorway networks. High tolls but fast and reliable.\n Iberian Peninsula (ES, PT):\nGood motorways with extensive tolling (Autopistas/Autoestradas). Mountain passes may restrict certain vehicle heights.\n Eastern Europe (PL, RO, BG, UA borders):\nSignificant investment in recent years but road quality and speed limits vary. Weight restrictions on secondary roads are common  especially in spring thaw periods (MarchMay).\n Balkan countries (RS, MK, BA, AL):\nLess developed infrastructure. Mountainous terrain. Lower average speed than Western corridors.\n Scandinavia (NO, SE, FI):\nWell maintained but seasonal challenges: winter closures, ferry requirements, and strict axle weight enforcement.\n\n\n3. Routing Tools and Software\n3.1 Professional Routing Software (Truck-Specific)\nStandard navigation applications such as Google Maps or Waze are not	500	[-0.04071045,-0.022109985,-0.008285522,0.0104522705,-0.028381348,0.012741089,0.036865234,0.0345459,-0.05831909,-0.01687622,0.040100098,-0.00674057,-0.02848816,-0.011390686,-0.025268555,0.014587402,0.011100769,-0.040863037,0.03237915,-0.042663574,0.0037631989,0.045898438,-0.034210205,-0.007827759,-0.025039673,-0.017333984,0.059265137,-0.007419586,-0.031082153,0.02279663,0.0052452087,0.022109985,0.017303467,-0.030944824,0.015426636,-0.044555664,0.038269043,-0.006580353,0.017974854,0.044067383,0.044891357,-0.019851685,0.017318726,0.070373535,-0.009414673,-0.014183044,-0.04473877,0.028366089,0.0040779114,-0.031402588,-0.04156494,-0.06964111,-0.024139404,0.0037345886,0.029510498,0.0129852295,0.024459839,0.0904541,-0.0008392334,0.031555176,0.008239746,-0.014419556,-0.02822876,-0.023864746,-0.034210205,0.03933716,0.016662598,0.011985779,-0.072631836,-0.04220581,-0.04940796,0.01763916,-0.010917664,0.011459351,0.002943039,-0.01576233,-0.0035533905,0.021240234,0.02670288,0.004447937,0.05340576,0.024795532,-0.0061149597,-0.041809082,0.0020961761,-0.021118164,-0.039794922,-0.09637451,0.037322998,0.0070991516,0.0029754639,-0.009757996,-0.053588867,0.02330017,0.030929565,0.0046157837,-0.004814148,-0.001958847,0.025756836,0.0035934448,0.007221222,-0.018936157,0.014404297,0.008056641,0.045043945,-0.015701294,0.015159607,0.0039138794,-0.04296875,0.038269043,0.057403564,-0.019317627,0.046142578,0.03945923,-0.033416748,-0.044799805,-0.021865845,-0.06976318,0.05935669,0.055511475,-0.020614624,0.009727478,0.013633728,-0.035369873,-0.056610107,0.029510498,-0.028289795,0.012779236,0.051605225,