2ab36e12-b168-4ed4-a7f0-b55b58939fce	59050f63-61ce-4125-9dc1-8c1b20f09f54	7ba430b5-849e-48e7-aba9-902af6db4577	8	ursions  coordinate precise appointment times.\n\nHazardous Materials (ADR)\nTransport of dangerous goods across Europe is governed by the ADR Agreement (European Agreement concerning the International Carriage of Dangerous Goods by Road). As a dispatcher:\n You must know the ADR class of the cargo before planning  verify with the shipper.\n The driver must hold a valid ADR certificate for the specific class of hazmat.\n The vehicle must be equipped with the correct safety equipment (fire extinguishers, warning signs, personal protective equipment).\n Certain ADR classes are banned from specific tunnels, city zones, and ferry routes.\n Tunnel categories AE restrict different ADR classes  always check before routing through tunnels.\n\n? Note: Always inform your driver about hazmat tunnel restrictions before they depart. Entering a restricted tunnel with ADR cargo can result in serious fines and mandatory escort.\n\n6.2 Weight Distribution and Axle Loading\nOne of the most common compliance errors new dispatchers make is approving a load without verifying axle weight distribution. A trailer can be within total GVW limits while individual axles exceed legal limits due to uneven cargo placement.\n\nKey Principles of Weight Distribution\n Cargo must be placed to ensure even axle loading  heavier items closer to the centre of the trailer.\n For a standard 13.6m trailer: optimal cargo placement distributes weight so the drive axles carry ~3035% and the trailer axles carry ~3540% of total load.\n Liquid cargo (tankers) requires additional calculations for dynamic weight shifts during braking and cornering.\n Always request a loading plan from the shipper for partial loads or palletized mixed cargo.\n\n?  If unsure about axle loading, use a certified weighbridge before departure. Weighbridge checks are available at most major truck stops and are mandatory at certain border crossings (e.g., entering Turkey).\n\n6.3 Trailer Selection Guide\n\nTrailer Type\nCargo Types\nKey Considerations\nCurtainsider (Tautliner)\nPalletized goods, machinery, timber, boxed cargo\nSide-loading. Most versatile  90%+ of European general freight.\nBox / Closed Van\nHigh-value goods, electronics, clothing, pharma\nSide doors only. Better security and weather protection.\nReefer (Refrigerated)\nFood, pharmaceuticals, flowers, temperature-sensitive cargo\nATP cert	500	[-0.022903442,-0.0079422,-0.0014667511,0.0026073456,-0.01158905,-0.011192322,-0.016204834,0.025527954,-0.06774902,-0.009498596,0.042755127,-0.010093689,-0.0178833,-0.015731812,-0.03994751,0.005874634,0.0034675598,-0.009216309,0.016311646,-0.035491943,0.04586792,0.027877808,0.008239746,-0.0034637451,0.021347046,0.003358841,0.019729614,9.9003315e-05,-0.0077171326,0.027008057,0.01235199,0.050476074,-0.0019054413,-0.033691406,0.01902771,-0.040771484,-0.006778717,-0.00068712234,-0.007335663,0.015655518,-0.011543274,-0.015525818,-0.027526855,0.045898438,-0.020767212,-0.006603241,-0.029144287,0.033721924,-0.0015764236,-0.014801025,-0.047027588,-0.07537842,-0.033050537,0.015426636,0.023590088,0.026306152,-0.006095886,0.12011719,-0.0069618225,-0.0026760101,-0.014678955,-0.04284668,-0.012687683,-0.0066223145,-0.04724121,0.0335083,0.009567261,0.03363037,-0.03050232,0.0005130768,-0.051239014,0.015602112,-0.050445557,0.028396606,-0.0032310486,-0.02104187,-0.002199173,0.057037354,0.04940796,0.004257202,0.052581787,0.027511597,0.009468079,0.006465912,0.034484863,-0.014511108,-0.068237305,-0.103271484,0.054534912,-0.0064201355,0.028839111,-0.0104599,-0.0071144104,-0.017486572,0.01121521,0.0042266846,-0.017028809,0.0047798157,0.037750244,-0.025604248,0.0064315796,-0.0063972473,0.0054626465,0.0039482117,0.029159546,-0.016662598,0.03640747,-0.0063285828,-0.015975952,0.052490234,0.013786316,-0.0076026917,0.03994751,0.016342163,-0.011291504,-0.077819824,-0.029556274,-0.068237305,0.02055358