8ace5b9f-51fb-453e-ac1a-302f8e979181	59050f63-61ce-4125-9dc1-8c1b20f09f54	7ba430b5-849e-48e7-aba9-902af6db4577	11	 a consistent workflow. Skipping steps leads to costly errors, delays, and compliance violations. Use this process as your standard operating procedure:\n\nStep 1: Receive and Review the Load Inquiry\n Confirm commodity type (is it standard, hazmat, temperature-controlled, oversized?)\n Note collection and delivery addresses  use full postal codes\n Confirm requested pickup and delivery date/time windows\n Identify any special requirements: tail lift, crane, ADR, multi-drop, etc.\n\nStep 2: Check Driver and Vehicle Availability\n Review driver hours remaining (check ELD/tachograph data)\n Verify driver's licence category, ADR certification (if required), and medical fitness\n Check vehicle: is the trailer type correct? When was last maintenance? Is the tachograph calibrated?\n Confirm vehicle dimensions match load requirements\n\nStep 3: Plan the Route\n Enter vehicle profile into routing software\n Set departure date/time  software will flag weekend bans and driving time limits\n Identify rest stops and overnight parking (use Truck Parking Europe app or similar)\n Calculate realistic ETA accounting for: driving time, mandatory breaks, border crossings, loading/unloading\n Calculate toll costs and note them for rate verification\n\nStep 4: Verify Compliance\n Check cabotage count if any domestic legs are involved\n Verify load falls within weight and dimension limits for all countries en route\n Confirm required documents are prepared or can be obtained before departure\n Check for active road closures, construction, or weather advisories on the route\n\nStep 5: Brief the Driver\n Share the route plan digitally  do not rely on verbal instructions alone\n Communicate: pickup address, contact name & phone, time window, and load instructions\n Communicate: delivery address, contact name & phone, time window, and any special unloading requirements\n Confirm driver understands driving ban times applicable to their route\n Confirm driver has all required documents or knows where to collect them\n\nStep 6: Monitor and Manage\n Track vehicle position via TMS or telematics system\n Check in with driver at key milestones: after loading, at border crossings, at rest stops if running late\n Proactively notify customer if ETA is at risk  do not wait for the customer to chase you\n Update TMS	500	[0.03225708,-0.005432129,-0.0019130707,-0.005809784,-0.045135498,0.0007534027,0.016021729,0.049316406,-0.04901123,0.005050659,0.07305908,-0.01423645,-0.032226562,0.017150879,0.016983032,0.013595581,-0.013679504,-0.024276733,0.0020580292,-0.012306213,0.022262573,0.03781128,-0.004940033,0.043151855,-0.010299683,-0.010643005,0.03640747,0.0011434555,-0.017593384,0.019012451,0.013252258,0.05706787,-0.03604126,-0.026748657,0.024475098,-0.007827759,0.008926392,-0.02520752,0.0028858185,0.013175964,0.013084412,0.004989624,0.008483887,0.047088623,-0.016998291,-0.008399963,-0.038970947,0.019470215,-0.028015137,0.013877869,-0.005970001,-0.04812622,-0.020584106,-0.02015686,0.025863647,0.008964539,0.025390625,0.041870117,0.0011119843,-0.02746582,-0.0064086914,-0.044952393,-0.0062828064,-0.02973938,-0.024383545,0.03012085,0.01184082,0.013839722,-0.006702423,-0.00091552734,-0.07397461,-0.0362854,-0.03086853,0.03427124,-0.011398315,-0.009757996,0.01550293,0.022338867,0.08294678,-0.015426636,0.030349731,-0.00548172,0.039978027,-0.000197649,0.039367676,0.024536133,-0.027908325,-0.081970215,0.02532959,0.008003235,0.014793396,-0.041748047,-0.0050315857,0.0012111664,0.018737793,0.011947632,-0.013557434,0.005783081,0.008430481,-0.042053223,-0.018554688,-0.042663574,-0.014785767,-0.005718231,0.040222168,-0.021026611,0.020233154,-0.0043411255,0.0020999908,0.019073486,0.035858154,-0.01586914,0.037994385,0.011367798,-0.026916504,-0.052856445,-0.0059318542,-0.06311035,0.011985779,-0.02281189,0.016204834,0.009567261,-0.007843018,0.0187