d6ff266f-0d44-4194-b06b-cb279a619145	59050f63-61ce-4125-9dc1-8c1b20f09f54	7ba430b5-849e-48e7-aba9-902af6db4577	12	 Check in with driver at key milestones: after loading, at border crossings, at rest stops if running late\n Proactively notify customer if ETA is at risk  do not wait for the customer to chase you\n Update TMS with real-time status and any exceptions\n\nStep 7: Close the Load\n Confirm delivery completion and collect POD (Proof of Delivery  signed CMR)\n Scan and upload POD to TMS within 24 hours of delivery\n Log any incidents, damages, or exceptions in the TMS\n Initiate driver debrief if any route deviation, delay, or issue occurred\n\n?  Consistent use of this 7-step workflow reduces errors, improves on-time performance, and creates a clear audit trail for every load. Senior dispatchers complete all 7 steps instinctively  new dispatchers should use a printed checklist until the workflow is second nature.\n\n\n\n9. Fuel Planning and Cost Management\n9.1 Fuel Prices Across Europe\nFuel is typically the single largest operating cost for a truck, accounting for 2535% of total trip costs. Smart fuel planning can save hundreds of Euros on a single run. As a dispatcher, you should guide drivers to fuel at the most cost-effective locations on their route.\n\nRegion / Country\nRelative Diesel Price Level\nDispatcher Advice\nLuxembourg ????\nLowest in Western Europe\nFuel up fully if routing through. Major truck fuel stop hub.\nPoland / Czech Republic\nLower than Western EU average\nFuel up on eastbound journeys before entering Germany or Austria.\nGermany / Austria / Belgium\nMid-high range\nTop up if necessary but avoid filling completely if cheaper country is close.\nScandinavia (NO, SE, FI)\nAmong the highest in Europe\nPre-fuel in Germany or Denmark before entering. Monitor AdBlue too.\nSwitzerland\nHigh  plus road toll costs\nPre-fuel in Germany (Basel area) before entering Switzerland.\nTurkey / Ukraine / Balkan non-EU\nVariable  sometimes cheaper, quality varies\nCaution on fuel quality. Stick to established truck stop chains if possible.\n\n9.2 Fuel Cards and Tolling Cards\nMajor European fuel card and fleet card providers allow drivers to pay for fuel and tolls without carrying cash. As a dispatcher, you should know which cards your company uses and their network coverage:\n DKV Mobility:\nLargest European network. Covers fuel, tolls	500	[-0.00020670891,0.0056648254,-0.012687683,0.017120361,-0.03289795,0.0006108284,0.007331848,0.03286743,-0.06890869,0.009536743,0.03591919,-0.035217285,-0.025177002,-0.014259338,-0.03756714,-0.011375427,-0.0032100677,-0.021377563,0.019241333,-0.018035889,0.0012159348,0.023757935,-0.0023612976,-0.029190063,-0.03363037,-0.0035209656,0.019241333,0.019821167,-0.0060424805,0.01701355,-0.010414124,0.047058105,-0.02949524,-0.03967285,0.01826477,-0.027526855,0.011558533,-0.021453857,0.034240723,0.026855469,0.0018339157,-0.008850098,0.0035686493,0.019943237,-0.0057754517,-0.02835083,-0.030227661,0.036376953,0.0026874542,-0.003156662,-0.0317688,-0.11004639,-0.0413208,-0.00067043304,0.02230835,0.017715454,-0.023529053,0.09667969,-0.0074806213,-0.0059432983,-0.008918762,-0.041015625,0.006996155,-0.023971558,-0.03933716,0.036102295,-0.019622803,0.035308838,-0.03652954,-0.006942749,-0.052642822,0.034240723,-0.012756348,0.033325195,-0.014305115,-0.020019531,0.011245728,-0.005443573,0.030822754,0.003921509,0.049743652,0.024047852,0.015296936,-0.0079574585,0.022750854,0.009857178,-0.060699463,-0.1005249,0.027679443,-0.0034885406,0.007549286,-0.031951904,-0.061065674,0.006549835,0.013473511,0.010406494,-0.017974854,0.013549805,0.018188477,-0.006538391,0.012565613,-0.0309906,0.0009775162,0.020858765,0.07122803,-0.019470215,0.030853271,-0.03753662,-0.010124207,0.01927185,0.040527344,-0.004837036,0.0070877075,0.05166626,-0.0031471252,-0.048950195,0.01134491,-0.08807373,0.016845703,0.016845703,-0.018478394,-0.015914917,0.034332275,0.026763916,-0.04574585,0.042297363,-0.0038280487,-0.0098