210ec694-13f3-467e-853d-657d3b9df08b	59050f63-61ce-4125-9dc1-8c1b20f09f54	7ba430b5-849e-48e7-aba9-902af6db4577	13	 and fleet card providers allow drivers to pay for fuel and tolls without carrying cash. As a dispatcher, you should know which cards your company uses and their network coverage:\n DKV Mobility:\nLargest European network. Covers fuel, tolls, parking, ferry, and washing in 50+ countries. Preferred card for pan-European operations.\n UTA Edenred:\nStrong coverage across Western and Central Europe. Includes German Maut, Swiss LSVA, and French Telepeage.\n Esso/BP/Shell FleetCard:\nBrand-specific but widely accepted. Useful as secondary cards on certain corridors.\n Eurotoll (EETS):\nEuropean Electronic Tolling Service provider. Single device covers tolls across multiple countries.\n\n10. Communication in Cross-Border Operations\n10.1 Communicating with Drivers in Multiple Languages\nEuropean dispatchers frequently work with drivers from various countries  Polish, Romanian, Bulgarian, Ukrainian, Lithuanian, and others are among the most common in European trucking. While English is widely used as the logistics lingua franca, clear communication must not be assumed.\n\nBest Practices for Cross-Language Driver Communication\n Use simple, short sentences and avoid idioms or slang.\n Provide written instructions (via TMS or WhatsApp) in addition to verbal communication  a driver can re-read a message but may forget a spoken instruction.\n Use address formats correctly  always include country code, postal code, city, and street. Avoid abbreviations.\n Confirm understanding by asking the driver to repeat key information back to you (pickup time, delivery address, contact phone).\n Build a glossary of key logistics terms in the most common driver languages your company uses (Polish, Romanian, Bulgarian, Lithuanian).\n\n10.2 Communicating with Shippers and Receivers\nShippers and receivers across Europe have different business cultures and communication expectations. Key principles:\n Always confirm appointments in writing (email or TMS message).\n Provide advance notice of any delay  minimum 2 hours before ETA if running late. For temperature-sensitive or time-critical loads, notify immediately.\n German, Austrian, and Swiss clients typically expect formal, precise communication. Brevity and accuracy are valued.\n Southern European contacts (Spanish, Italian, Greek) may prefer phone calls over emails  confirm preferred communication channel.\n Eastern European warehouses may have limited English  having contact numbers for	500	[-0.01739502,0.017288208,-0.01612854,0.016555786,-0.014656067,0.0121536255,0.012931824,0.022705078,-0.056915283,-0.013023376,0.03125,0.0010595322,-0.022354126,-0.03050232,-0.04623413,-0.006072998,-0.00074386597,-0.0008907318,-0.00034356117,0.0023403168,0.024841309,0.023895264,-0.021987915,-0.031082153,0.012123108,0.024429321,0.033416748,-0.0040283203,-0.016937256,0.018692017,-0.0131073,0.040252686,-0.017852783,-0.06628418,0.009605408,-0.051818848,0.0026378632,-0.03640747,0.038085938,0.022125244,0.0067863464,-0.013542175,0.033111572,0.027175903,-0.030822754,-0.012916565,-0.0126571655,0.022827148,-0.0071525574,-0.024368286,0.0008893013,-0.101989746,-0.02999878,0.0022468567,0.019042969,0.004169464,-0.017166138,0.05819702,0.041870117,-0.024871826,-0.019515991,-0.04647827,0.011001587,-0.051513672,-0.024215698,0.0619812,-0.01914978,0.043670654,-0.042510986,-0.0335083,-0.057128906,0.020721436,-0.037109375,0.052124023,-0.039978027,0.0067329407,0.023895264,0.018951416,0.044708252,-0.016357422,0.079711914,0.023788452,0.033477783,-0.020233154,0.02619934,-0.024749756,-0.05621338,-0.10040283,0.004928589,0.022079468,0.013389587,-0.035827637,-0.021957397,-0.021362305,0.011917114,-0.020828247,0.0028495789,-0.0047950745,-0.0042800903,-0.007209778,0.0045433044,-0.033203125,-0.0027809143,0.015319824,0.07519531,-0.03781128,-5.9604645e-06,-0.04574585,-0.010055542,0.06542969,0.025268555,0.004169464,0.041