0f9b70fe-a31c-4042-915a-ffb5cd6b9e98	59050f63-61ce-4125-9dc1-8c1b20f09f54	7ba430b5-849e-48e7-aba9-902af6db4577	14	 communication. Brevity and accuracy are valued.\n Southern European contacts (Spanish, Italian, Greek) may prefer phone calls over emails  confirm preferred communication channel.\n Eastern European warehouses may have limited English  having contact numbers for local logistics managers is essential.\n\n11. Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) for European Load Planning\nDispatcher performance in European operations is measured against several KPIs. Understanding these metrics helps new dispatchers prioritise the right activities:\n\nKPI\nTarget Benchmark\nHow to Improve\nOn-Time Pickup Rate\n>95%\nPlan realistic loading windows. Confirm appointments. Monitor driver position before pickup.\nOn-Time Delivery Rate\n>95%\nUse accurate routing, account for breaks and bans. Communicate proactively if at risk.\nEmpty Kilometres (Deadhead %)\n<15% of total km\nPlan return loads strategically. Use load boards for backhaul on every outbound trip.\nRevenue per km (/km)\nVaries by lane; target >1.50/km net\nOptimise lane selection and avoid low-yield lanes without backhaul potential.\nFuel Cost per 100km\nBenchmark vs fleet average\nGuide drivers to lower-cost fuel stops. Monitor fuel card data weekly.\nDriver Hours Utilisation\n>85% of available HOS used productively\nMinimise waiting time at shippers/receivers. Coordinate appointments precisely.\nPOD Collection Rate\n100% within 24h of delivery\nBrief drivers on POD importance. Chase missing PODs same day.\nCompliance Violations\n0 per quarter target\nAlways verify bans, cabotage, and weight compliance before dispatching.\n\n\n\n12. Quick Reference: Dispatcher Checklist\nPrint this page and keep it at your workstation as a daily reference until all steps become automatic.\n\n?\nPre-Dispatch Checklist Item\n?\nCargo type confirmed (standard / ADR / reefer / oversized)\n?\nDriver hours checked and sufficient for the load\n?\nVehicle profile entered correctly in routing software\n?\nWeekend / holiday driving bans checked for all countries on route\n?\nWeight and dimension limits verified for all countries on route\n?\nToll costs estimated and factored into load profitability\n?\nCabotage count checked (if domestic legs involved)\n?\nAll required documents prepared (CMR, invoice, ADR docs if applicable)\n?\nBorder crossing procedures confirmed (customs, transit docs)\n?\nDriver briefed: pickup details, route, delivery details, ban times\n	500	[0.0009303093,-0.018295288,-0.015304565,0.020217896,-0.041809082,-0.0040779114,0.0071487427,0.048339844,-0.061553955,0.015823364,0.053833008,-0.039611816,-0.013374329,-0.014595032,-0.04937744,-0.008026123,0.00018000603,-0.031311035,0.0051345825,-0.0005197525,0.037017822,0.039855957,-0.01474762,0.0016422272,0.010536194,0.003036499,0.027069092,0.011482239,0.025924683,0.015548706,-0.0056266785,0.052581787,-0.018371582,-0.06390381,0.010986328,-0.03125,0.0025081635,-0.03729248,0.025238037,0.0093307495,-0.007572174,0.0066184998,0.0129776,0.04119873,-0.016052246,-0.014030457,-0.009170532,0.015701294,-0.015327454,0.0023937225,0.004272461,-0.09136963,-0.038085938,-0.009033203,0.013282776,0.018493652,0.005317688,0.050994873,0.023666382,-0.010757446,-0.022369385,-0.049438477,0.010887146,-0.032806396,-0.043151855,0.049621582,-0.014221191,0.0395813,-0.01197052,-0.0058250427,-0.0317688,0.00012362003,-0.029632568,0.048950195,-0.03074646,-0.033599854,-0.014022827,0.022766113,0.062438965,-0.004764557,0.062683105,0.007507324,0.0010690689,0.008460999,0.056884766,-0.021713257,-0.041870117,-0.1171875,0.030731201,-0.005622864,0.019592285,-0.027832031,-0.021743774,-0.032928467,0.021957397,-0.0027770996,-0.005897522,-0.010871887,0.025512695,-0.029571533,0.00080776215,-0.04562378,0.010322571,-0.0049476624,0.047790527,-0.013587952,0.015640259,-0.02822876,-0.020721436,0.014343262,0.02281189,-0.006801605,0.039123535,0.028274536,-0.015411377,-0.0546875,-0.00683593