734c2199-e5a3-4656-b39e-9385c8898df9	a3a6df7a-b369-4a43-bb23-c9277fec93b2	7ba430b5-849e-48e7-aba9-902af6db4577	0	\nDispatcher Onboarding Guide\nIndustry Fundamentals for European Truck Transportation\n\nThis onboarding guide is designed to provide new dispatchers with a strong foundation in the European road transportation industry. The document introduces industry terminology, daily operations, regulations, transport documentation, and professional expectations.\n\n================================================================================\nPAGE 1 - INTRODUCTION TO THE EUROPEAN ROAD TRANSPORT INDUSTRY\n================================================================================\n\nWhat Is Road Freight Transportation?\n-----------------------------------\nRoad freight transportation is the movement of goods using trucks across cities and countries. In Europe, trucking is one of the most important parts of the supply chain because it connects manufacturers, warehouses, ports, retailers, and customers. Many industries depend on road transport for fast and reliable deliveries. Truck transportation supports both domestic and international trade and is essential for supermarkets, factories, construction sites, and e-commerce operations.\n\nThe Role of a Dispatcher\n------------------------\nA dispatcher coordinates daily transport activities between drivers, customers, warehouses, carriers, and internal operational teams. Dispatchers assign loads to drivers, monitor vehicle movements, communicate delays, solve operational problems, and ensure legal compliance. A dispatcher must remain organized, calm under pressure, and capable of handling multiple shipments simultaneously.\n\nMain Types of Transport\n-----------------------\nThe most common transport types include:\n- Full Truck Load (FTL)\n- Less Than Truck Load (LTL)\n- Express transport\n- Refrigerated transport\n- ADR transport for dangerous goods\n\nFTL shipments usually involve one customer per truck, while LTL combines multiple customer shipments. Refrigerated transport is used for temperature-sensitive goods such as food or pharmaceuticals.\n\nIndustry Participants\n---------------------\nImportant participants in the transport industry include:\n- Shippers\n- Freight forwarders\n- Carriers\n- Drivers\n- Warehouses\n- Customs authorities\n- Customers\n\nAll parties must cooperate effectively to ensure successful transport operations.\n\n================================================================================\nPAGE 2 - HOW EUROPEAN TRUCK TRANSPORTATION WORKS\n================================================================================\n\nInternational Transport Operations\n----------------------------------\nEuropean truck transportation is highly interconnected. Trucks regularly cross multiple countries during one trip. Dispatchers must coordinate border crossings, toll systems, delivery appointments, customs requirements, and driver working hours. Delays at one location can affect the entire transport schedule.\n\nMain European Transport Corridors\n---------------------------------\nMajor transport corridors connect key logistics regions across Europe. Examples include:\n- Germany-France\n- Germany-Poland\n- Benelux-Italy\n- Spain-France\n- Central Europe-Balkans\n\nMajor logistics hubs such as Rotterdam	500	[-0.009063721,0.0031967163,-0.016464233,-0.0010814667,-0.032806396,-0.03717041,0.014884949,0.025054932,-0.04953003,0.010116577,0.024551392,-0.03274536,0.017074585,-0.036102295,-0.055633545,0.02420044,-0.016860962,-0.01525116,0.029663086,-0.024658203,0.070495605,0.05883789,-0.043640137,-0.0037078857,-0.013259888,-0.0038890839,0.04248047,0.008804321,-0.0013599396,0.013755798,-0.011817932,0.0473938,-0.017745972,-0.067993164,0.018295288,-0.0135650635,0.004371643,-0.007183075,0.0013389587,-0.005077362,-0.0073928833,0.008674622,0.015220642,0.045532227,-0.016235352,-0.011383057,-0.02305603,0.03942871,-0.0129470825,0.015487671,-0.0076904297,-0.064575195,-