78c8b3a9-d076-476e-8d96-8c0f66840865	c5021bcd-8030-4b72-8101-82ff232ff7c0	7ba430b5-849e-48e7-aba9-902af6db4577	0	\nDISPATCHER TRAINING PROGRAM\nCommunication Skills\nfor Truck Dispatchers\nTalking to Drivers  ·  Customers  ·  Brokers  ·  Emergency Situations\n\nVersion 1.0  |  2024  |  Confidential  Internal Training Document\n\n\n1\nWhy Communication Is the Dispatcher's Core Skill\n\nA dispatcher who can plan perfect routes but communicates poorly will consistently underperform a dispatcher who is merely good at planning but excellent at communicating. Every operational outcome  on-time delivery, driver safety, customer satisfaction, and profitable freight  depends on clear, timely, and professional communication.\n\nAs a dispatcher in truck transportation, you are the nerve centre of a complex operation. At any given moment you are simultaneously managing:\n Drivers on the road who need instructions, support, and real-time problem-solving\n Customers and shippers who expect precise ETAs and proactive updates\n Brokers and freight partners with whom you negotiate rates and confirm load details\n Internal teams including operations managers, maintenance, and accounts\n Authorities and third parties when incidents, delays, or compliance issues arise\n\n1.1 What Good Dispatcher Communication Looks Like\nHigh-performing dispatchers share a consistent set of communication behaviours regardless of the channel they are using  phone, radio, TMS message, WhatsApp, or email:\n\nPrinciple\nWhat It Means in Practice\nClarity\nOne message = one clear meaning. No ambiguity about what you need or when you need it.\nBrevity\nSay what matters, then stop. Drivers are driving. Customers are busy. Long messages lose people.\nAccuracy\nNever guess and present it as fact. If you are not sure  say so, then find out and follow up.\nTimeliness\nCommunicate before the other person needs to ask. Proactive beats reactive every time.\nTone\nProfessional but human. You get more from people through respect than through pressure.\nConfirmation\nClose every important exchange with a summary of what was agreed and who does what next.\n\n1.2 The Cost of Poor Communication\nCommunication failures in trucking are not abstract  they have direct financial and operational consequences. Studies across European logistics operators consistently show that communication breakdowns account for a significant share of operational failures:\n Missed pickups and deliveries due to incorrect address, wrong contact, or no advance notice of schedule change\n Driver confusion leading to wrong routes, unauthorised stops, or undelivered	500	[-0.004005432,-0.02607727,-0.0017414093,0.025680542,-0.010307312,0.0038032532,0.019821167,0.039978027,-0.0692749,-0.0031013489,0.029800415,0.004837036,0.019104004,-0.033935547,-0.027420044,0.015167236,-0.011253357,0.01928711,0.019241333,0.028045654,0.008125305,0.0135650635,-0.06414795,-0.006702423,-0.01247406,0.0061035156,0.015151978,0.0093307495,-7.247925e-05,-0.023742676,-0.032409668,0.03237915,-0.015213013,-0.064575195,0.026824951,-0.02999878,-0.004184723,-0.044647217,0.0021915436,0.028411865,-0.017166138,-0.017303467,0.033599854,0.0008921623,0.008308411,-0.0027008057,-0.026885986,0.011749268,-0.011123657,-0.015274048,-0.012962341,-0.097717285,-0.022979736,0.010879517,0.03274536,0.047973633,0.041107178,-0.033081055,0.030456543,-0.03656006,-0.021331787,-0.046020508,0.02607727,-0.032562256,-0.032196045,0.040649414,-0.03982544,0.05569458,-0.02897644,-0.025497437,-0.03363037,0.005092621,-0.04031372,0.055664062,-0.023834229,-0.009246826,0.04159546,0.05831909,0.018249512,-0.040893555,0.07824707,0.012718201,0.007785797,0.0073509216,0.06262207,-0.016662598,-0.05908203,-0.111694336,0.04260254,0.02168274,0.005466461,-0.019958496,0.008270264,-0.0070495605,0.005870819,0.00057697296,0.023269653,-0.0053634644,0.008010864,-0.0075950623,0.026519775,-0.02999878,0.0013418198,0.03137207,0.018844604,-0.019470215,-0.00920105,-0.021957397,0.015510559,