130a97a7-7962-45df-a902-a9136c713d44	c5021bcd-8030-4b72-8101-82ff232ff7c0	7ba430b5-849e-48e7-aba9-902af6db4577	6	 able to reach a person, not just reply to an email.\n Response time: Customer emails during business hours should receive a reply within 2 hours maximum. Urgent issues: call, do not email.\n\n\n5\nBroker and Freight Partner Communication\n\nFreight brokers connect available capacity with shippers who need transport. Your relationship with brokers directly affects the quality and volume of freight your trucks can access. Strong broker communication builds a reputation for reliability  and reliable carriers get first access to the best loads.\n\n5.1 First Contact and Load Confirmation\nWhen responding to a broker about a posted load, speed and clarity are critical. Brokers often contact multiple carriers simultaneously and award loads to whoever responds first with a complete, professional answer.\n\nResponding to a Load Offer (Phone)\nBroker\nHi, I have a load from Warsaw to Dusseldorf, 24t, pickup Tuesday, delivery Thursday. Can you do it?\nDispatcher\nGood afternoon. Yes, we have a Euro 6 curtainsider available for Tuesday morning. Just to confirm: pickup in Warsaw from when exactly, and what's the delivery window in Dusseldorf? Also  what rate are you working with?\nBroker\nPickup from 08:00, delivery Thursday before 12:00, rate is 1,200 all-in.\nDispatcher\nUnderstood. We can confirm at 1,200 all-in. I'll need the full shipper address, contact name, and CMR instructions. Can you send the rate confirmation to operations@fastfreight.eu? Once received I'll confirm driver details back to you within the hour.\n\n5.2 Negotiating Rates Professionally\nRate negotiation is a regular part of a dispatcher's work. The goal is not to win every negotiation  it is to reach a number that works for both sides quickly and without damaging the relationship.\n\n Know your floor before you pick up the phone. Calculate your full cost (fuel, tolls, driver hours, empty return) and know the minimum rate at which the load is viable. Never negotiate without this number.\n Anchor first when possible. The first number in a negotiation tends to anchor the conversation. If you have to make an offer, open slightly above your target.\n Use silence strategically. After stating your rate, stop talking. Silence is not agreement  and filling it prematurely often leads to concessions you don't need to make.\n Trade concessions, don't just	500	[-0.0073165894,-0.049102783,-0.0032424927,0.018753052,0.0046463013,0.0055122375,0.0064964294,0.04421997,-0.060150146,0.029205322,0.027618408,0.014160156,-0.0045814514,-0.025177002,-0.023468018,0.00088500977,0.015792847,0.013465881,-0.028656006,-0.006164551,0.033355713,0.05630493,-0.011672974,-0.015113831,-0.023345947,-0.013114929,0.012863159,0.00022244453,-0.015655518,-0.0048217773,0.0002939701,0.048217773,-0.030181885,-0.0209198,0.0049438477,-0.035064697,-0.036346436,-0.048431396,0.02986145,0.002691269,-0.012817383,-0.01121521,0.025253296,-0.028900146,-0.030838013,-0.0020866394,-0.016906738,0.029647827,0.024963379,-0.010307312,0.0051231384,-0.058898926,-0.029159546,-0.0015001297,0.02418518,0.020248413,0.023544312,0.025512695,0.002248764,-0.032562256,0.020706177,-0.05218506,0.0026283264,-0.032073975,-0.045288086,0.07055664,-0.005317688,0.064941406,-0.07196045,-0.020126343,-0.062347412,-0.0053520203,-0.053009033,0.057922363,-0.014953613,0.020141602,0.030838013,0.044006348,0.048217773,0.0033473969,0.061706543,0.040039062,0.039520264,-0.031921387,0.011047363,-0.04763794,-0.041381836,-0.10089111,0.040740967,0.07904053,0.011604309,-0.03286743,-0.0357666,-0.017044067,-0.0034980774,-0.020568848,-0.0058898926,0.003047943,0.0022888184,-0.03225708,0.00819397,-0.000518322,-0.01928711,0.026168823,0.031707764,-0.0008764267,-0.017501831,-0.02720642,-0.033294678,0.06542969,0.016784668,0.0143966675,0.026992798,0.009544373,0.0024261475,0.03491211,-0.010238647,-0.029769897,0.035125732,-0.026123047,-0.0047187805,-0.016