c564392f-10b4-462b-bf4f-ce614e96d6bc	1d5e7c69-2edd-4e9e-a9ca-d37f7f473864	389ac876-e11d-4d4d-8914-58f9295fd59c	1	 doses.\nRare side effects (may affect up to 1 in 1000 people):\n- Skin rash or allergic reaction\n- Low blood pressure if given by injection (not applicable for tablets)\n\nVery rare side effects:\n- Blood disorders including thrombocytopenia (low platelet count)\n- Abnormal liver function tests with prolonged high-dose use\n\nIf you notice any side effects not listed here, contact your doctor or pharmacist.\n\nSTORAGE\n-------\n- Store below 25°C in a dry place\n- Keep out of the direct sunlight\n- Keep out of the reach and sight of children\n- Do not use after the expiry date printed on the packaging\n- Do not store in a bathroom or near a sink\n\nOVERDOSE INFORMATION\n--------------------\nOverdose with paracetamol is dangerous.\nSymptoms of overdose may include: nausea, vomiting, and abdominal pain.\nLiver damage may occur 24 to 72 hours after overdose and may not produce symptoms initially.\nIf overdose is suspected, seek emergency medical attention immediately.\nThe antidote for paracetamol overdose is N-acetylcysteine (NAC), which is most effective when given within 8 to 10 hours of ingestion.\n\n\n\n\nLEGAL CATEGORY\n--------------\nGeneral Sale (GSL) - available without prescription\nPack sizes available: 16, 32 tablets\n	274	[-0.034484863,0.024612427,0.01550293,0.07244873,0.021362305,0.006919861,-0.05178833,-0.022735596,0.0030918121,-0.0049324036,0.03173828,-0.020965576,-0.016464233,-0.058776855,0.03302002,0.059539795,-0.040222168,-0.02406311,-0.01235199,0.021240234,0.051330566,-0.018920898,0.03253174,0.0065841675,0.013763428,0.04055786,-0.015159607,0.0027484894,0.014343262,0.03540039,-0.045135498,-0.015205383,-0.02394104,0.018157959,0.02281189,0.010131836,0.007534027,-0.004234314,0.04815674,0.034088135,0.009246826,0.025497437,-0.042663574,-0.013687134,-0.06829834,-0.029525757,0.041534424,-0.0037574768,-0.0016527176,-0.009750366,-0.018493652,-0