ndications\nDo NOT take Paracetamol 500mg tablets if you meet any of the following conditions:\n- Allergic to paracetamol or any other ingredient in this product.  \n- Have severe liver disease.  \n- Have severe kidney disease.  \n- Are already taking other products containing paracetamol.  \n\n---\n\n### Warnings\nTo ensure safe use of Paracetamol, keep the following precautions in mind:\n- **Do Not Exceed Dose:** Taking more than the recommended dose can cause serious liver damage, which may not be apparent for several days.  \n- **Overdose Action:** If an overdose is taken, go immediately to the nearest hospital emergency department, even if you feel well.  \n- **Avoid Combination:** Do not take with other paracetamol-containing products.  \n- **Consult a Doctor:** Seek medical advice before use if you are taking warfarin (a blood-thinning medicine).  \n\n---\n\n### Side Effects\nParacetamol is generally well tolerated at recommended doses. However, some rare or very rare side effects may occur:\n\n#### Rare Side Effects (May Affect Up to 1 in 1000 People)\n- Skin rash or allergic reaction.  \n- Low blood pressure (if given by injection, not applicable for tablets).  \n\n#### Very Rare Side Effects\n- Blood disorders, including thrombocytopenia (low platelet count).  \n\n--- \n\nBy following these guidelines, you can ensure the safe and effective use of Paracetamol 500mg Tablets. Always consult a healthcare professional if you have questions or concerns.
