COPY public.questions (id, project_id, question_text, option_a, option_b, option_c, option_d, correct_answer, explanation, is_published, module_id, learning_path_id) FROM stdin;
94e5580a-b3ae-4117-bee9-1a863887d02e	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	What is the primary characteristic of a unicorn startup?	A) A startup that has gone public	B) A startup valued at over $1 billion	C) A startup with global expansion	D) A startup focused on AI platforms	B	A unicorn is defined as a privately owned startup valued at over $1 billion.	t	a2abf46d-5301-4b31-a074-19ca805b5770	cb14a137-4265-4ba3-a9d7-42b0de847a28
6257828a-06da-45f0-a68c-eaaa296212b9	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	Which funding stage typically involves individual investors providing early capital to startups?	A) Series A	B) Angel investors	C) Seed round	D) IPO	B	Angel investors are individuals who provide early-stage funding to startups, often before formal funding rounds like Seed or Series A.	t	a2abf46d-5301-4b31-a074-19ca805b5770	cb14a137-4265-4ba3-a9d7-42b0de847a28
6359f598-7c6a-49cd-9cae-7ac07c9abed7	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	What does 'burn rate' refer to in startup funding?	A) The rate at which a startup spends its capital	B) The time taken to achieve product-market fit	C) The percentage of equity diluted in funding rounds	D) The valuation growth rate of a startup	A	'Burn rate' refers to the rate at which a startup spends its available capital, which is critical for determining its financial runway.	t	a2abf46d-5301-4b31-a074-19ca805b5770	cb14a137-4265-4ba3-a9d7-42b0de847a28
89b18bb5-c833-44b2-b525-c10c5559af47	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	What is the primary goal of achieving product-market fit in a startup?	A) To validate that the product satisfies market demand	B) To secure funding from venture capitalists	C) To scale the startup globally	D) To automate business processes	A	Achieving product-market fit ensures that the product meets the needs of the target market, which is critical for the startup's success before scaling or seeking funding.	t	d834b2ec-c3e2-409a-8043-3b910531ce23	cb14a137-4265-4ba3-a9d7-42b0de847a28
7afaa453-0ce1-4678-8e3c-839b124dd68b	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	Which of the following is NOT a common strategy for scaling a unicorn startup?	A) Hiring engineering teams	B) Using cloud infrastructure	C) Ignoring global expansion	D) Leveraging AI/data-driven growth	C	Ignoring global expansion is not a strategy for scaling; global expansion is often a key factor in a unicorn's growth.	t	d834b2ec-c3e2-409a-8043-3b910531ce23	cb14a137-4265-4ba3-a9d7-42b0de847a28
c115ecfb-b2c7-4451-9ab7-2b869441a11d	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	Why do most startups fail according to the Unicorns Learning Path?	A) Lack of funding	B) Failure to achieve product-market fit	C) Poor cloud infrastructure	D) Ineffective marketing	B	Most startups fail because they do not achieve product-market fit, which is essential for validating the idea and ensuring market demand.	t	d834b2ec-c3e2-409a-8043-3b910531ce23	cb14a137-4265-4ba3-a9d7-42b0de847a28
0ba1afe1-f1e7-41b6-b6f5-2205d070de90	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	What is a key focus when analyzing real unicorns?	A) Studying their founding story, funding rounds, architecture, monetization, failures, and pivots	B) Learning about their tech stack only	C) Understanding their advanced topics like FinOps and distributed systems	D) Focusing solely on their IPO process	A	Analyzing real unicorns involves studying their founding story, funding rounds, architecture, monetization, failures, and pivots to understand how they achieved their success.	t	60401ede-d4ee-4317-94cd-d67d62a44694	cb14a137-4265-4ba3-a9d7-42b0de847a28
4363f567-bb9f-49a5-86b0-5bceaa68f370	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	Which of the following companies is considered a good case study for analyzing real unicorns?	A) Airbnb	B) Kubernetes	C) Terraform	D) Azure	A	Airbnb is listed as one of the recommended companies to study when analyzing real unicorns, along with Databricks, Revolut, and Notion.	t	60401ede-d4ee-4317-94cd-d67d62a44694	cb14a137-4265-4ba3-a9d7-42b0de847a28
32c958ef-8e92-4bd4-8601-2bebaa806503	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	What is NOT a suggested aspect to study when analyzing real unicorns?	A) Founding story	B) Monetization	C) Cloud infrastructure	D) Failures and pivots	C	Cloud infrastructure is part of scaling unicorns, but analyzing real unicorns focuses on aspects like founding story, monetization, and failures/pivots.	t	60401ede-d4ee-4317-94cd-d67d62a44694	cb14a137-4265-4ba3-a9d7-42b0de847a28
14a4cd60-7339-4bf4-b896-7074997e318d	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	What is a recommended tech stack for building your own mini unicorn project?	A) Python + FastAPI, React/Next.js, PostgreSQL, Docker, Azure	B) Ruby on Rails, Angular, MySQL, Kubernetes, AWS	C) Java + Spring Boot, Vue.js, MongoDB, Docker, Google Cloud	D) PHP + Laravel, Svelte, SQLite, Kubernetes, IBM Cloud	A	The recommended stack for building a mini unicorn project includes Python + FastAPI for backend, React/Next.js for frontend, PostgreSQL for database, Docker for containerization, and Azure for cloud infrastructure.	t	008bdb76-e226-4ae3-8665-1ad3aeae565b	cb14a137-4265-4ba3-a9d7-42b0de847a28
c96243b7-7f25-44da-a5de-206acd415e3a	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	Which type of project is suggested for creating your own mini unicorn?	A) AI assistant	B) E-commerce platform	C) Social media app	D) Cryptocurrency exchange	A	The learning material recommends creating projects like SaaS apps, AI assistants, workflow automation platforms, or internal enterprise tools as part of building a mini unicorn project.	t	008bdb76-e226-4ae3-8665-1ad3aeae565b	cb14a137-4265-4ba3-a9d7-42b0de847a28
87fe9118-5f57-47a2-8cab-72286711b96e	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	What is the timeline suggested for building your own MVP in the Unicorns Learning Path?	A) Week 1	B) Week 2	C) Week 3	D) Week 4	D	The suggested timeline in the learning path allocates Week 4 for building your own MVP after covering startup basics, funding, product-market fit, scaling, and studying real unicorns.	t	008bdb76-e226-4ae3-8665-1ad3aeae565b	cb14a137-4265-4ba3-a9d7-42b0de847a28
c289c43b-5115-4a44-ab6a-dbc0a4d68d11	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	What is a common technology stack used by unicorns for scaling their operations?	A) Kubernetes and Terraform	B) Lean startup methodology	C) Bootstrapping and Angel investors	D) MVP and product-market fit	A	Kubernetes and Terraform are examples of technologies used in cloud infrastructure and automation, which are essential for scaling operations in unicorn startups.	t	6d5a71a1-b7c6-4982-bfe6-09e823b519cb	980f4dbe-2a2f-4dcc-8777-25d6927b9b80
c3e54847-4380-419e-8c65-39d86c91ec6a	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	What is a key factor that makes scaling possible for unicorns, as discussed in the learning material?	A) Equity dilution	B) Multi-tenant SaaS architecture	C) Cloud infrastructure	D) Bootstrapping	C	Cloud infrastructure is a critical factor that enables unicorns to scale globally and efficiently, as highlighted in the learning material under 'How Unicorns Scale'.	t	5c300589-bc72-4b57-93fb-cb9761e89fc3	980f4dbe-2a2f-4dcc-8777-25d6927b9b80
c80daf46-178e-4165-844b-fe540b411727	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	Which of the following is NOT a key strategy for scaling unicorn startups?	A) Cloud infrastructure	B) DevOps & automation	C) MVP (Minimum Viable Product)	D) Global expansion	C	MVP (Minimum Viable Product) is a fundamental concept for startup validation, not specifically a scaling strategy for unicorns. Scaling strategies focus on infrastructure, automation, and global growth.	t	6d5a71a1-b7c6-4982-bfe6-09e823b519cb	980f4dbe-2a2f-4dcc-8777-25d6927b9b80
d8575832-69bb-4880-88d7-0657e471c368	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	Which of the following is NOT a reason why most startups fail?	A) Lack of product-market fit	B) Poor financial management	C) Overinvestment in cloud infrastructure	D) Ineffective growth strategies	C	While cloud infrastructure is important for scaling, overinvestment in it is not typically cited as a primary reason for startup failure. Most failures stem from issues like lack of product-market fit, poor financial management, or ineffective growth strategies.	t	e2eb8976-4213-41d3-a2d9-a86c66b59647	980f4dbe-2a2f-4dcc-8777-25d6927b9b80
