3cded944-6773-4de0-8cfe-cfb024f598bf	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	What is the maximum number of cabotage operations a foreign carrier can perform within 7 days after completing an international delivery in an EU country?	A) 2	B) 3	C) 5	D) Unlimited	B	EU Regulation 1072/2009 specifies that a foreign carrier may perform a maximum of 3 cabotage operations within 7 days of completing an international delivery in the country.	t	da9fd45c-582d-41c0-88a7-fcaeda88d35b	a6c704ca-ebad-46a5-b7bb-eb4b2d6a0b35
52394061-5284-4db8-b7a2-3d8b3f12df07	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	Which European motorway serves as the main east-west backbone connecting Belgium, Germany, Poland, and Ukraine?	A) E35	B) E40	C) E75	D) E80	B	The E40 motorway is identified as the main east-west backbone connecting Belgium, Germany, Poland, and Ukraine.	t	8a62e608-b5e7-4c25-a9bb-085d27e1247e	a6c704ca-ebad-46a5-b7bb-eb4b2d6a0b35
5318dbbb-19a4-4e26-9123-3dee8c2e6438	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	What is a recommended practice for communicating with drivers in multiple languages during cross-border operations?	A) Use idioms and slang for clarity	B) Provide written instructions in addition to verbal communication	C) Only use verbal communication for faster understanding	D) Avoid confirming understanding to save time	B	Providing written instructions (via TMS or WhatsApp) in addition to verbal communication allows drivers to re-read and retain the information, especially when working in a multilingual environment.	t	803a30dc-016c-4894-9551-6460602c30ea	a6c704ca-ebad-46a5-b7bb-eb4b2d6a0b35
6404da30-03d7-4140-abbc-aaa078e7698f	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	What must dispatchers consider when routing hazardous materials (ADR) through tunnels?	A) Tunnel categories restrict different ADR classes and must be checked before routing.	B) Tunnels are universally accessible to ADR cargo.	C) ADR cargo is only restricted in ferry routes, not tunnels.	D) Drivers can decide tunnel access based on their judgment.	A	Tunnel categories (A-E) restrict different ADR classes; dispatchers must verify restrictions before routing hazardous materials through tunnels.	t	f3d5a019-013f-4a0f-b76c-e766115ebcb7	a6c704ca-ebad-46a5-b7bb-eb4b2d6a0b35
6c3e4403-c3bc-4585-b344-6cd9c8ec44ea	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	Which of the following factors is unique to European load planning compared to domestic trucking?	A) Cabotage restrictions	B) Uniform axle load limits	C) Consistent tolling systems across countries	D) Single language communication	A	Cabotage restrictions are specific to the European freight market, limiting how many loads a foreign carrier can perform within a single country, unlike domestic trucking.	t	8a62e608-b5e7-4c25-a9bb-085d27e1247e	a6c704ca-ebad-46a5-b7bb-eb4b2d6a0b35
75f0ff83-110f-4e26-bebc-fb644478d01a	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	Which European country has a maximum vehicle height limit of 4.9 meters for practical purposes?	A) Netherlands	B) Switzerland	C) United Kingdom	D) Nordic countries	C	The UK has a practical maximum vehicle height limit of 4.9 meters, though there is no EU-wide law on maximum height.	t	da9fd45c-582d-41c0-88a7-fcaeda88d35b	a6c704ca-ebad-46a5-b7bb-eb4b2d6a0b35
7b5bde9a-302d-4631-9e04-1a16974684a8	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	Which document is required for hazardous goods transportation and includes details such as the UN number, class, and packing group?	A) Phytosanitary Certificate	B) ADR Documentation	C) EUR.1 Movement Certificate	D) Green Card	B	ADR Documentation is specifically required for hazardous goods transportation and includes critical safety details such as the UN number, class, and packing group.	t	e14a34cf-57bf-4c96-808a-7abaac79a79c	a6c704ca-ebad-46a5-b7bb-eb4b2d6a0b35
880ea25f-1ac8-435e-9831-68c542d93ce7	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	Which toll payment system is widely used in France for barrier-free payment on motorways?	A) LSVA System	B) Liber-t / Télépéage	C) Toll Collect System	D) RoLa Piggyback	B	The Liber-t / Télépéage transponder system allows barrier-free payment on French motorways and is compatible with most major European transponder providers.	t	a372395b-2342-4acc-ba40-fda043a43070	a6c704ca-ebad-46a5-b7bb-eb4b2d6a0b35
5723271e-e0b3-42cb-97e6-79523faf86e9	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	Which European road corridor serves as the main east-west backbone for cross-border trucking?	A) E17	B) E40	C) E75	D) E55	B	The E40 corridor, spanning Belgium, Germany, Poland, and Ukraine, is the main east-west backbone for cross-border trucking in Europe.	t	faca4d20-f745-4054-8f4e-84951f5a59e2	a0517415-7f58-4971-b5fa-83e96abe68e7
89b531fd-d352-4208-a43c-a083596b7060	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	Which digital load board has the largest European presence with over 750,000 transport offers daily?	A) Teleroute	B) Bursa de Freight	C) TimoCom (TC Truck & Cargo)	D) Transopedia	C	TimoCom (TC Truck & Cargo) is the largest load board in Europe, offering over 750,000 transport options daily across 44 countries.	t	62ce837f-4790-4a20-b296-95f5189dbbf0	a6c704ca-ebad-46a5-b7bb-eb4b2d6a0b35
2f0364d1-e3a1-4112-a1e4-a2721701c98c	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	What is the recommended communication method for drivers who may forget spoken instructions?	A) Use verbal instructions only	B) Provide written instructions via TMS or WhatsApp	C) Use idioms and slang for clarity	D) Rely on phone calls for all communication	B	Providing written instructions ensures drivers can re-read the message if they forget spoken instructions, enhancing clarity and reducing errors.	t	f211ee5b-7712-4048-b99a-9e9b49a3433f	a0517415-7f58-4971-b5fa-83e96abe68e7
02f8ccbd-60b8-4144-b8dd-5da85f507f05	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	How should dispatchers handle communication with Southern European shippers and receivers?	A) Only use formal emails	B) Confirm preferred communication channels, often phone calls	C) Avoid providing advance notice of delays	D) Use idioms and slang to build rapport	B	Southern European contacts often prefer phone calls over emails, and dispatchers should confirm their preferred communication channel to ensure effective interaction.	t	f211ee5b-7712-4048-b99a-9e9b49a3433f	a0517415-7f58-4971-b5fa-83e96abe68e7
125210b1-070c-4549-a1a4-1a266adbaeb3	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	What should be confirmed with the driver after delivery?	A) Pickup details	B) POD collection	C) Route information	D) Ban times	B	The checklist specifies that POD (Proof of Delivery) collection should be confirmed with the driver after delivery.	t	0fc4468d-75a9-4b72-905d-b599f8436614	a0517415-7f58-4971-b5fa-83e96abe68e7
6f4b908a-e2cb-4ef9-9c9c-0bdffd147dda	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	What must be uploaded to the TMS within 24 hours of delivery?	A) Route details	B) Driver's ETA	C) POD	D) Border crossing procedures	C	The checklist requires that the POD (Proof of Delivery) be uploaded to the TMS within 24 hours of delivery.	t	0fc4468d-75a9-4b72-905d-b599f8436614	a0517415-7f58-4971-b5fa-83e96abe68e7
f4da1056-b22a-4e37-8d6c-4d4fa5b2937c	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	Which of the following is part of the driver briefing process?	A) Tracking enabled in TMS	B) Pickup details, route, delivery details, ban times	C) Customs and transit documents	D) Uploading POD to TMS	B	The checklist specifies that the driver should be briefed on pickup details, route, delivery details, and ban times.	t	0fc4468d-75a9-4b72-905d-b599f8436614	a0517415-7f58-4971-b5fa-83e96abe68e7
ad20309f-6b82-4378-a8a0-b98a577e2ce8	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	Which professional routing software is specifically designed for driver navigation and includes offline maps and trailer profiles?	A) Sygic Truck GPS	B) PTV Navigator / PTV Map&Guide	C) HERE WeGo Truck	D) TomTom Telematics	A	Sygic Truck GPS is tailored for driver navigation and provides offline maps, trailer profiles, and parking spot features.	t	62ce837f-4790-4a20-b296-95f5189dbbf0	a6c704ca-ebad-46a5-b7bb-eb4b2d6a0b35
c22265f5-1c62-4ce2-a5d9-5e900c01d86b	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	How is Switzerland's LSVA toll fee calculated for heavy vehicles over 3.5 tonnes?	A) Based on GVW only	B) Total distance driven × GVW × emission class factor	C) Flat rate per truck	D) Number of axles × emission class factor	B	Switzerland's LSVA toll fee is calculated using the formula: total distance driven in Switzerland × gross vehicle weight (GVW) × emission class factor.	t	a372395b-2342-4acc-ba40-fda043a43070	a6c704ca-ebad-46a5-b7bb-eb4b2d6a0b35
cc910205-cbb9-42f1-a20e-617814f460a7	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	What is a key principle of weight distribution for a standard 13.6m trailer?	A) Drive axles should carry ~30-35% and trailer axles ~35-40% of total load.	B) Heavier items should be placed at the rear of the trailer.	C) Liquid cargo requires no special considerations.	D) Axle weight distribution is not necessary for compliance.	A	Optimal cargo placement ensures even axle loading, with drive axles carrying ~30-35% and trailer axles ~35-40% of the total load.	t	f3d5a019-013f-4a0f-b76c-e766115ebcb7	a6c704ca-ebad-46a5-b7bb-eb4b2d6a0b35
eae0f0f1-3346-431c-8d70-e3455590494a	791553e4-9051-47cc-84c5-ef11694ee801	What factors determine the toll rate for trucks in Germany's SS Toll System?	A) Distance traveled, emission class, and number of axles	B) Truck weight only	C) Distance traveled and fuel type	D) Number of drivers in the vehicle	A	The toll rate in Germany's SS Toll System is calculated per kilometer based on the truck's EURO emission class, the number of axles, and the distance traveled.	t	a372395b-2342-4acc-ba40-fda043a43070	a6c704ca-ebad-46a5-b7bb-eb4b2d6a0b35
37669a5d-512f-4320-8993-7c76c640c7f0	389ac876-e11d-4d4d-8914-58f9295fd59c	Which of the following individuals should NOT take Paracetamol 500mg tablets?	A) Someone with a headache	B) Someone with severe liver disease	C) Someone over 16 years old	D) Someone with cold symptoms	B	Paracetamol 500mg tablets are contraindicated for individuals with severe liver disease due to the risk of serious liver damage.	f	df16504d-6886-462c-866b-87f5f69d6645	25bfe6a5-74f5-4732-8e0d-e031ebf5b99a
