cbde6cc5-6039-441b-8159-92999011be2c	389ac876-e11d-4d4d-8914-58f9295fd59c	Which of the following is a rare side effect of Paracetamol 500mg tablets?	A) Skin rash or allergic reaction	B) Nausea and vomiting	C) Abdominal pain	D) Low blood pressure when taken orally	A	Skin rash or allergic reaction is listed as a rare side effect of Paracetamol 500mg tablets, occurring in up to 1 in 1000 people. Nausea, vomiting, and abdominal pain are symptoms of overdose, not regular side effects. Low blood pressure is a rare side effect but only applicable if given by injection, not orally.	f	dfe5caab-5403-433a-81c8-57e016ad0d31	25bfe6a5-74f5-4732-8e0d-e031ebf5b99a
ba6655a3-1f21-4be4-af06-f5b82aaaf91a	389ac876-e11d-4d4d-8914-58f9295fd59c	What is the correct way to store the medication?	A) Below 25°C in a dry place, away from direct sunlight	B) In a bathroom or near a sink	C) Above 25°C in a humid environment	D) In the refrigerator at 4°C	A	The medication should be stored below 25°C in a dry place, away from direct sunlight, and out of the reach and sight of children, as per the provided storage instructions.	f	5de245ff-9c5a-43d5-bf54-f3459e3d5f87	25bfe6a5-74f5-4732-8e0d-e031ebf5b99a
69c1d1af-7079-4ea6-9e4b-529d487d0f5b	389ac876-e11d-4d4d-8914-58f9295fd59c	What is the recommended antidote for a paracetamol overdose?	A) Activated charcoal	B) N-acetylcysteine (NAC)	C) Vitamin K	D) Aspirin	B	N-acetylcysteine (NAC) is the recommended antidote for paracetamol overdose, as it is most effective when administered within 8 to 10 hours of ingestion.	f	43dbc0f9-f1ee-4fea-9fcb-9d5a67f976aa	25bfe6a5-74f5-4732-8e0d-e031ebf5b99a
b209db25-5c5b-4efd-a374-f1eb53a57edf	389ac876-e11d-4d4d-8914-58f9295fd59c	What is the legal category of the product as described in the material?	A) Prescription Only Medicine (POM)	B) General Sale (GSL)	C) Pharmacy Medicine (P)	D) Controlled Drug (CD)	B	The product is categorized as General Sale (GSL), meaning it is available without a prescription.	f	18aa33c1-c17f-487b-b134-dc100618adf5	25bfe6a5-74f5-4732-8e0d-e031ebf5b99a
6c8803f1-0c91-4fe3-97b2-cfe05c1d1c82	389ac876-e11d-4d4d-8914-58f9295fd59c	What is the maximum number of Paracetamol 500mg tablets an adult can take in 24 hours?	A) 6 tablets	B) 8 tablets	C) 10 tablets	D) 12 tablets	B	Adults can take a maximum of 8 tablets (4000mg) in any 24-hour period, as stated in the dosage guidelines.	f	25d45f6d-f000-4e76-ace7-413b4b5ed71f	896d0dc9-2bb8-4e06-a2c2-4f8804d8f788
