de7ae0c0-b64b-4408-aecb-a4613e90ae88	389ac876-e11d-4d4d-8914-58f9295fd59c	For which of the following conditions should Paracetamol 500mg tablets NOT be used?	A) Headache	B) Sore throat	C) Severe liver disease	D) Muscle aches	C	Paracetamol 500mg tablets are contraindicated for individuals with severe liver disease, as mentioned in the contraindications section.	f	75cfb78a-55c5-44e5-804c-e0115dcdfff7	896d0dc9-2bb8-4e06-a2c2-4f8804d8f788
86989ae3-d35a-403c-a9c4-5ec77e00a5b9	389ac876-e11d-4d4d-8914-58f9295fd59c	Which of the following is a contraindication for taking Paracetamol 500mg tablets?	A) Severe liver disease	B) Mild headaches	C) Muscle aches	D) Cold and flu symptoms	A	Paracetamol 500mg tablets are contraindicated for individuals with severe liver disease as noted in the patient information leaflet.	f	77de4cd6-771a-4173-a2d3-77df759ecf21	896d0dc9-2bb8-4e06-a2c2-4f8804d8f788
e3b97387-f43b-46c9-b1ab-4dfffee71180	389ac876-e11d-4d4d-8914-58f9295fd59c	What should you do if you accidentally take more than the recommended dose of Paracetamol 500mg tablets?	A) Wait to see if symptoms develop	B) Drink water and rest at home	C) Immediately go to the nearest hospital emergency department	D) Take another dose to counteract the overdose	C	The leaflet warns that overdose can cause serious liver damage, and it is crucial to seek emergency medical attention immediately even if you feel well.	f	77de4cd6-771a-4173-a2d3-77df759ecf21	896d0dc9-2bb8-4e06-a2c2-4f8804d8f788
3fa80475-05ae-49a2-af29-53b2ed5d642c	389ac876-e11d-4d4d-8914-58f9295fd59c	Which of the following is considered a rare side effect of Paracetamol 500mg tablets?	A) Skin rash or allergic reaction	B) Nausea and vomiting	C) Abdominal pain	D) Fever	A	Skin rash or allergic reaction is listed as a rare side effect of Paracetamol 500mg tablets, occurring in up to 1 in 1000 people.	f	337d193d-0f70-43f2-9140-944b3242d064	896d0dc9-2bb8-4e06-a2c2-4f8804d8f788
